# Soldering at tool stations (decision C17): the DIP into the vise; arm
# A picks a resistor while the positioner brings pin 3's tip to the
# stations' working point, turned and tilted so the iron's and the
# feeder's lines are clear; arm A brings the resistor's lead to it; station S1's iron extends onto the
# joint, station S2 feeds solder into it, the iron backs away and the
# joint freezes; the resistor stays, soldered on.
reset circuit=demo
tool A tweezers
pick A U1 grasp=ends
place A U1 at=0,0,-32 rpy=0,0,90
vise close
release A U1
lift A mm=60
pick A R1 grasp=body
present U1.3.tip at=S1 and=S2
move A to=40,60,60
align A R1.1.tip to=U1.3.tip gap=0.1
touch S1 at=U1.3+R1.1 dwell=2
feed S2 mm=2 rate=1
back S1
wait until=U1.3+R1.1 below=100
inspect U1.3+R1.1
release A R1
lift A mm=40
